      "text": "Sarvottam Cables (NSE: SRVCABLE) manufactures power cables, wires and conductors.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E2"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "Q1 FY27 consolidated revenue from operations was ₹1,248 crore, up 18.0% year-on-year.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E4"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "Profit after tax for Q1 FY27 was ₹82 crore, up 5.9%.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E7"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "EBITDA margin was 11.2%, down 170 basis points from 12.9% in Q1 FY26.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E6"}]
    }
  ],
  "Bull case": [
    {
      "text": "Order book stood at ₹3,900 crore as of 30 June 2026, up from ₹3,150 crore a year earlier.",
      "citations": ["S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E8"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "The company says its Bharuch plant, adding about 30% to cable capacity, is on track for Q3 FY27 commercial production; management expects data-centre cables, currently about 9% of domestic revenue, to double within two years.",
      "citations": ["S3", "S2"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E10"}, {"id": "S2:E3"}]
    }
  ],
  "Bear case": [
    {
      "text": "EBITDA margin fell 170 bps to 11.2% as copper rose nearly 14%; the MD attributes this mostly to copper, with price-variation clauses covering two-thirds of contracts resetting on a one-to-two-quarter lag.",
      "citations": ["S3", "S1", "S2"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S3:E6"}, {"id": "S1:E4"}, {"id": "S2:E6"}, {"id": "S2:E7"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "The CFO confirmed receivable days rose from 78 to 96 over the last year, mainly from two large state-utility customers.",
      "citations": ["S2"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S2:E11"}, {"id": "S2:E12"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "The company disclosed a ₹46.3 crore CGST demand (including interest and penalty) on FY2020-21 and FY2021-22 input tax credit and intends to file an appeal.",
      "citations": ["S7"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S7:E1"}, {"id": "S7:E2"}]
    }
  ],
  "Open questions": [
    {
      "text": "Revenue conflict: S1 (news) reports ₹1,428 crore at 35% growth while the official filing (S3) reports ₹1,248 crore at 18.0% for Q1 FY27; the official figure is preferred.",
      "citations": ["S1", "S3"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S1:E2"}, {"id": "S3:E4"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "A March 2024 news report cited promoter pledge at 35% of promoter holding; the latest NSE filing (June 2026) shows 4.1% of promoter holding pledged, making the 2024 figure historical rather than a current contradiction.",
      "citations": ["S4", "S8"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S4:E1"}, {"id": "S8:E2"}]
    },
    {
      "text": "With a one-to-two-quarter pass-through lag on price-variation clauses and receivable days now at 96, how quickly will cash collection adjust if copper costs remain elevated?",
      "citations": ["S2"],
      "evidence": [{"id": "S2:E7"}, {"id": "S2:E11"}]
    }
  ]
}
